{"ev": "setup-screen", "step": 0, "shot": "tablet-landscape-celestial_en__setup0.png", "key": "943f1865c5", "labels": ["Location: ⁨⁩. Opens location settings", "Saturday 17 October 2026  ·  9:49 AM", "·", "⁨٦ جمادى الأولى ١٤٤٨⁩", "Learn Salah", "Monthly timetable", "Settings", "Designed by UZR  ·  Make duʿā for me", "Step 1 of 4: Welcome", "ميقات", "English", "اردو · Urdu", "As-salāmu ʿalaykum", "Miqaat is a prayer clock. It calculates the five daily prayer times on this device for the place you choose, plays the azaan, and can count down to iqamah for prayer at home.  Nothing is uploaded: there is no account, no advertising and no analytics. Two things use the network — the optional place-name lookup (Android's geocoder, run by Google) and the update check on GitHub in the direct-download edition. Both are off until you use them.", "Setup takes about a minute: your place → check the times → azaan alerts.", "Begin"], "clickables": ["Learn Salah", "Monthly timetable", "Settings"], "t": 7.7}
